label ch30_6:
    [   0] m "By the way, there's something that's been bothering me..."
    [   1] m "You know how this takes place in Japan?"
    [   2] m "Well...I assume you knew that, right?"
    [   3] m "Or at least decided it probably does?"
    [   4] m "I don't think you're actually told at any point where this takes place..."
    [   5] m "Is this even really Japan?"
    [   6] m "I mean, aren't the classrooms and stuff kind of weird for a Japanese school?"
    [   7] m "Not to mention everything is in English..."
    [   8] m "It feels like everything is just there because it needs to be, and the actual setting is an afterthought."
    [   9] m "It's kind of giving me an identity crisis."
    [  10] m "All my memories are really hazy..."
    [  11] m "I feel like I'm at home, but have no idea where 'home' is in the first place."
    [  12] m "I don't know how to describe it any better..."
    [  13] m "Imagine looking out your window, but instead of your usual yard, you're in some completely unknown place."
    [  14] m "Would you still feel like you were home?"
    [  15] m "Would you want to go outside?"
    [  16] m "I mean...I guess if we never leave this room, it doesn't really matter anyway."
    [  17] m "As long as we're alone and safe together, this really is our home."
    [  18] m "And we can still watch the pretty sunsets night after night."
